<Item XName="Flexible OFDM Source Measurement" UserName="Flexible OFDM Source Measurement" Type="Notes">
<Description>Example text with pretty printing</Description>
<LibName>Eagleware</LibName>
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 1pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; mso-element: para-border-div; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .75pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0in; TEXT-ALIGN: center; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .75pt; mso-padding-alt: 0in 0in 1.0pt 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Flexible&amp;nbsp;OFDM Source Measurement&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;This example workspace demonstrates the&amp;nbsp;generation of MIMO flexible OFDM signal. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Various OFDM waveforms can be generated by SystemVue FlexOFDM Application. One flexible OFDM frame consists of idle, preamble (Preamble 1 and Preamble 2) and payload data (Data 1 and Data 2) including pilots. By using different configuration, users can get different OFDM frames according to their requirement.&amp;nbsp; In FlexOFDM_EVM model, Preamble1 is used for synchronization and the default data of Preamble1 are the same in different antennas. If the data of Preamble1 are not the same in different antennas, synchronization performance degradation would appear (in FlexOFDM_MIMO_4x4 Type 0). Preamle2 or Pilots could be chosen to do channel estimation.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 9pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; COLOR: #333333; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;Preamble 2 can be switched ON or OFF. Data 2 (Payload 2) also can be turn ON or OFF. There are only the Data 1 (Payload 1) and the Preamble1 which should be always presence for receiver.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;The output of FlexOFDM_MIMO_Source is connected to VSA software from which we can see the spectrum and demodulation performance&amp;nbsp;in VSA custom OFDM system. Parameter should be&amp;nbsp;consistent&amp;nbsp;with that&amp;nbsp;in VSA. Please&amp;nbsp;refer to&amp;nbsp;the document in VSA for detail. Configuration files generated by FlexOFDM_MIMO_Source&amp;nbsp;can make the connection&amp;nbsp;with VSA much easier.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Simulation Instruction&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To get the simulation run, the following parameters should be set properly.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;1.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;In MIMO page of UI on FlexOFDM_MIMO_Source_RF, &#x2018;NumOfSubcarriersPerBlock&#x2019; should be set as the divisor of &#x2018;NumUsefulSubcarriers&#x2019;. &#x2018;NumOfSymbolsPerBlock&#x2019; should be set as the divisor of &#x2018;NumOfSym&#x2019;.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;2.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;In Preamble page of UI on FlexOFDM_MIMO_Source_RF, the length of &#x2018;Preamble_CarrierIndex&#x2019; should be consistent with the value in &#x2018;Preamble_NumOfCarriers&#x2019;. The parameter &#x2018;Preamble1_Seq&#x2019; and &#x2018;Preamble2_Seq&#x2019; are the value of Preamble in all antennas, and the data are mapping to the location in the sequence of antenna 1, antenna 2 and so on. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;3.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;In Data page on FlexOFDM_MIMO_Source_RF, &#x2018;Data_NumOfCarriers&#x2019; could be an array, the element of the array is the number of data carriers per symbol. The length of &#x2018;Data_NumOfCarriers&#x2019; should be set as the divisor of &#x2018;NumOfSym&#x2019;. &#x2018;Data_CarrierIndex&#x2019; should be consistent with the value in &#x2018;Data_NumOfCarriers&#x2019;.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;4.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;In Pilot page on FlexOFDM_MIMO_Source_RF, the value of parameter &#x2018;Pilot1_Seq&#x2019; are the value of pilots in all antennas, and the value are mapping to the location in the sequence of antenna 1, antenna 2 and so on.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;5.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;In MIMO page of UI on FlexOFDM_MIMO_Receiver_RF, two kinds of the structure on Preamble2 and pilots are provided according to LTE system (Non-Overlapping) and WLAN system (Overlapping). If Preamble2 is chosen to estimate the channel, only Overlapping type is available.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;6.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;In RxAlgorithm page of UI on FlexOFDM_MIMO_Receiver_RF, Preamble2 or pilots is chosen to do channel estimation by parameter &#x2018;PilotsBasedChannelEst&#x2019;. &#x2018;PhaseTrackingEnable&#x2019; is available when channel estimation is based on Preamble2.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;7.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-tab-count: 1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;When the synchronization performance degradated, smaller value of PeakThreshold in FlexOFDM_EVM model will make it easier to get the frame synchronization.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;8.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Please change the parameters in the equation for the consistency of FlexOFDM_MIMO_Source and FlexOFDM_EVM. If parameters are changed by GUI, please change the parameters in FlexOFDM_MIMO_Source and FlexOFDM_EVM at the same time.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;9.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Parameter &apos;PrecodingEnable&apos; is not supported without the feedback of receiver. If &apos;PrecodingEnable&apos; is set to &apos;Yes&apos;, please make sure the input port &apos;MIMOPrecoding&apos; is connected.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;10. The value of Parament &apos;Pilot1_Seq&apos; of FlexOFDM_MIMO_4x4 is set by function &apos;randn&apos;, which makes the output of FlexOFDM_MIMO_Souce different in every simulation. Change to the values of pilots to constant may make the&amp;nbsp;output of FlexOFDM_MIMO_Souce keep the same.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;There are two designs in this example. One is for MIMO 2x2 and the other is 4x4. The maximum anttena number in VAS is 4. In each Equation, two&amp;nbsp;types of parameter setting are given.&amp;nbsp; One type is called non-overlapping in VSA which is MIMOType = 0&amp;nbsp;in FlexOFDM_EVM. The other is&amp;nbsp;called Overlapping in VSA which is MIMOType =&amp;nbsp;1&amp;nbsp;in FlexOFDM_EVM. Please make sure the number of symbols is bigger than NumOfTx in Overlapping mode. Please make sure the &apos;QAM_Identifiers&apos; and the &apos;QAM Levels&apos; is consistent with that in VSA.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;In FlexOFDM_MIMO_Source_RF GUI, when Generate Configuration File is enabled, the corresponding files for VSA demoudalation will be generated. In these two examples, after VSA 89600 software is invoked, users need to load these generated files in VSA Custom OFDM Demod UI for Pilot IQ , Preamble IQ, Resource Map and Resouce Modulation respectively.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Arial&apos;&gt;Things to Try&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in 1.2pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-add-space: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;1.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT: 7pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Try two different pilots pattern and using VSA to do demodulation. 1x1, 2x2 and 4x4 are supported in VSA. See the spectrum, demodulation constellation and EVM in VSA.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in 1.2pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-add-space: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;2.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT: 7pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Try different parameter such as modulation, pilots pattern, frame structure and demodulation methods and see the influence on EVM.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
